Sval: a blocked embed's placeholder asks Sval before it loads

The placeholder's button notifies a topic Sval's protection button answers
with a prompt, in place of opening Firefox's protections panel. A page can
send its shim's messages itself (Shims._onMessageFromShim), so the page asks
and the browser decides. Allowing sends Firefox's own
smartblock:unblock-embed for each embed the page's content-blocking log
shows replaced, as the protections panel's toggles do.

diff --git a/browser/extensions/webcompat/experiment-apis/trackingProtection.js b/browser/extensions/webcompat/experiment-apis/trackingProtection.js
index 125dc12dc5..c13e32bca8 100644
--- a/browser/extensions/webcompat/experiment-apis/trackingProtection.js
+++ b/browser/extensions/webcompat/experiment-apis/trackingProtection.js
@@ -310,7 +310,7 @@ this.trackingProtection = class extends ExtensionAPI {
           let win = tab?.window;
           Services.obs.notifyObservers(
             win.gBrowser.selectedBrowser.browsingContext,
-            "smartblock:open-protections-panel"
+            "sval-smartblock-embed-clicked"
           );
         },
         incrementSmartblockEmbedShownTelemetry() {
